course: dictionary
lesson: 15708
title: The torso
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The torso is the middle part of your body. When you name your head, arms and legs, the torso is the part left over. Your chest, stomach and back make up your torso.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The statue had a strong torso, but its head and arms were missing.» The head and arms are gone, so the torso must be the middle part that is still there. Check by swapping in your meaning: "The statue had a strong middle, but its head and arms were missing" still makes sense.
explain: «Ella twisted her torso to reach the ball.» Ella turned her middle, not her arms or legs. Twisting your torso means turning the middle of your body, so the word fits the action perfectly.
fact: The torso is the main part of the human body, not counting the head, arms and legs.
fact: The torso is made of the chest, stomach and back.
fact: «Torso» can also mean a statue of a body without a head, arms or legs.
fact: Many ancient Greek statues have been found broken, so only the torso is left.
fact: Your heart, lungs and stomach are inside your torso.
exercise: «The statue had a strong torso, but its head and arms were missing.» What is a torso? | A tall, thin tower | A small round stone | A pair of strong legs | *The main middle part of a body
exercise: Which part of your body holds your heart and lungs? | Your head | Your fingers | Your legs | *Your torso
exercise: «Ella twisted her torso to reach the ball.» Which part of Ella did she twist? | Her hair | Her legs | *Her middle body | Her head
test: What is a torso in an old statue? | A broken arm | A pair of legs | A small stone bench | *A body without its head, arms or legs
test: Which two parts are included in the torso? | Ears and nose | *Chest and stomach | Hands and feet | Knees and ankles
exam: Coach says, «Twist your torso slowly.» What should you move? | Your toes | *Your middle body | Your hands only | Your ears
